You are updating pages/HardFactsPage.tsx.

Locate the threatPoints array that contains:

const threatPoints = [
  "Missed calls don’t disappear — they go straight to your rivals.",
  "The customer you attracted — they get the sale.",
  // other items...
];


Locate the JSX where threatPoints is rendered, something like:

{threatPoints.map((point) => (
  <p className="...">
    {point}
  </p>
))}


Replace that .map block with this EXACT version so that
“The customer you attracted — they get the sale.” gets special styling:

{threatPoints.map((point, index) => {
  const isKeyLine =
    point === "The customer you attracted — they get the sale.";

  return (
    <p
      key={index}
      className={
        isKeyLine
          ? "mt-4 text-2xl md:text-3xl font-extrabold text-red-500 underline underline-offset-4 drop-shadow-md text-center"
          : "mt-2 text-lg md:text-xl font-medium text-blue-100"
      }
    >
      {point}
    </p>
  );
})}


RULES:

Do NOT change the text itself.

Do NOT change the threatPoints array contents.

Only replace the .map rendering block as shown.

Do not modify any other sections or components on the page.

After updating, rebuild/refresh so the new styles appear in the preview.
